    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d560">

                <pb facs="0690" n="376" xml:id="pg376"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 768.72/1388</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-27T16:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 27, 1914, 4 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>841. Our Embassy at Rome reports that British restrictions on shipping have
                    caused great irritation in Italy and that it seems a Change in feeling is
                        noticeable.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d560-f1"/> we have seen evidences of this
                    same irritation in taking with respresentatives of other neutral countries. You
                    can unofficially make this known to the Foreign Office in support of the
                    protests of American shippers. I have communicated the substance of this to the
                    British Embassy here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
